{"raw": "{
  "headline": "Bulk Sweep Incident Detected: Hundreds of New Hosts Logged in Simultaneously",
  "what_happened": "On Day 8, from 09:00 to 22:59, 322 logins were observed across 277 hosts by 55 users from 4 source hosts. The source hosts with the highest number of logins were C17693 (286), C3435 (31), C18025 (4), and C20427 (1). Users U66 (56), U8777 (39), U162 (24), U3635 (17), U293 (17), U1480 (14), and 49 more were also involved. Notably, 228 of these logins were the user's first-ever login to that host, and 304 were the source host's first-ever login to that host. The authentication method was predominantly NTLM (92%). The baseline for source host C17693 showed it was active on 4 out of 6 days, with about 13.0 new destinations per active day. User U66 was active on all 6 days, with about 1.5 new destinations per active day. The incident was flagged due to one source host reaching hundreds of new hosts at once, and one user reaching hundreds of new hosts at once. This incident was reviewed as a bulk sweep, with the rarest destinations including Assistant, C1022, C1035, C10794, C1086, and C1096.",
  "why_flagged": "The incident was flagged due to one source host reaching hundreds of new hosts at once, and one user"}
